      "content": "The Fourier transform decomposes a complex signal into its underlying constituent sine and cosine waves, allowing you to see exactly which frequencies are present and how strong they are. Physically, this is like shining a prism of light through a glass of water to separate a mixed beam into a rainbow of individual colors. By viewing your signal this way, you shift your perspective from how the values change over time to how different frequencies make up the whole, which is crucial for filtering noise or analyzing oscillations.",
